  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- H12c's logic is already fully correct per DS-4's audit. Extension -- N/A, config-only. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H12c blocks H14 (per DS-4 §4's DAG note); without confirming its credential config, the last handler in the integration-wiring wave (Wave G-6) cannot be reached even if every upstream handler works.</notes>

  <notes-completion>
    Investigated H12c's actual credential posture before touching anything (per Wave G-5 dispatch
    directive #2: "if code changes ARE needed, escalate before silently expanding scope").
    D-153-1: the POML's literal framing ("the customer-env Dataverse Web API credential it needs,
    matching the same H4-populated-KV pattern as H7/task 142") does NOT hold -- H12c's sole
    Dataverse Web API collaborator (DataverseWebApiModelDeploymentReferenceWriter.AcquireTokenAsync)
    already authenticates via DefaultAzureCredential(TenantId=...), the SAME UAMI-as-Dataverse-App-
    User idiom every OTHER post-H10 handler uses (H12a's 4 seeders, H12b's 2 seeders, H11, EntraAppReg,
    IntegrationWiring). H7 needed a client-secret specifically because it dispatches BEFORE H10 exists;
    H12c dispatches strictly after H12a+H12b, both themselves post-H10. No client-secret credential
    exists to provision -- confirms (does not conflict with) the Wave G-5 dispatch directive #4.

    D-153-2 (the genuine gap): RuntimeReferencesOptions.SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint (Model1Shared's
    shared-platform OpenAI endpoint -- a URL, not a secret) had ZERO Bicep app-setting wiring anywhere
    (grep-verified against both bicep files pre-task). Every Model1Shared customer's H12c run would
    fail Resumable forever until an operator noticed and hand-set an App Service setting. Wired
    RuntimeReferences__SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint as a KV-reference app setting on the Worker site,
    sourced from the SAME canonical "AzureOpenAI-Endpoint" KV secret the .Api site already resolves
    for AzureOpenAI:Endpoint / DocumentIntelligence:OpenAiEndpoint (per scripts/canonical-secret-
    catalog/manifest.yaml) -- single source of truth, not a duplicate. New param
    azureOpenAiEndpointSecretName (default 'AzureOpenAI-Endpoint', parity with bffApiClientSecretName's
    shape) on both modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep and platform-controlplane.bicep;
    threaded through the workerAppService module invocation; platform-controlplane.json regenerated
    via `az bicep build` (0 errors/0 warnings both files); set explicitly in
    parameters/platform-controlplane-dev.bicepparam. `az deployment sub what-if` (dev subscription):
    status "Succeeded", no errors -- Worker App Service shows as full "Create" (live-ceremony
    Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 has not run yet, identical to task 142's own finding -- not a regression).

    NFR-05: added RuntimeReferencesOptions.SectionName const ("RuntimeReferences", explicit-not-
    nameof per the established drift-prevention pattern) + internal Validate() bounds-checking ONLY
    DataverseRequestTimeout (1s-5m) -- deliberately does NOT require SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint at
    boot, because that field is CONDITIONALLY required (H12c's Model1Shared branch only); an
    unconditional boot requirement would crash-loop a Worker serving exclusively Model2Dedicated
    customers for a setting it never uses -- the NFR-05 pattern's failure mode in reverse. The
    existing per-run handler guard (already correct, already tested pre-task-153) remains the
    enforcement point for that field, correctly classified Resumable. Wired
    AddOptions<RuntimeReferencesOptions>().Bind().Validate().ValidateOnStart() inside
    RuntimeReferencesModule.AddH12cRuntimeReferencesHandler (parity with
    DataverseEnvironmentRegistryModule/task 122's shape) -- Program.cs's single
    AddH12cRuntimeReferencesHandler(...) call line is UNCHANGED (god-class-ratchet extension-method
    surface preserved). Verified no WorkerTestFactory placeholder was needed (unlike task 142's H7
    bonus-catch) because the bounds-only Validate() passes on RuntimeReferencesOptions's own defaults.

    Tests: added 6 new cases to H12cRuntimeReferencesHandlerTests.cs's new "NFR-05" region --
    OptionsValidate_Passes_With_Defaults_NoSharedPlatformEndpointRequired,
    _Passes_With_SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint_Set, _Throws_When_DataverseRequestTimeout_TooSmall
    (2 cases), _TooLarge, and a _SectionName_Is_RuntimeReferences regression-guard (parity with
    EnvVarValuesOptions's identical guard from task 142). 1061 -> 1067/1067 (+6, zero regressions,
    all pre-existing H12c test methods unmodified).

    Full deviation record: notes/task-153-h12c-credential-config-deviations.md (D-153-1/2/3).

    Step 9.5 (code-review + adr-check, test-modifying binding override applied since new tests were
    added): 0 Critical, 0 Warnings, 0 ADR violations across ADR-004/010/028/032/036 -- no new
    interfaces (ADR-010), no hardcoded secrets / KV-ref reuses existing canonical secret name
    (ADR-028), no feature-gate branch introduced (ADR-032 unconditional registration preserved),
    no BFF-hygiene trigger (L2 control-plane only, not src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**).
  </notes-completion>

